# The Windows launcher is run by `cmd`, which mis-parses a batch file whose
# lines end with LF alone — a line can end mid-token and the file silently does
# the wrong thing. `-text` keeps the CRLF the bundler writes, on checkout and
# on commit, whatever the user's core.autocrlf says.
*.cmd -text
*.bat -text

# The packed runner is binary; never let a line-ending filter near it.
*.tgz binary
